        "reason": "The installed model grosses household VAT up to receipts by a single factor of 0.38 (gov.simulation.microdata_vat_coverage). policyengine-uk #2187 divides instead by survey consumption coverage times the household share of VAT receipts, 0.67 \u00d7 0.7 = 0.469, so this model's VAT is about 23% higher (the UK hub's notice 59 puts it about 24% high on Microcosm), and a measure that moves a VAT rate, the VAT base or the consumption VAT is charged on can be overstated by as much. A measure built with the VAT base template is held too, though the term the template adds is not grossed. #2187 is not in this model. Until a pair with it is adopted, such measures are held at provisional."
